On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:05:27 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:
>> Setting notmuch-archive-tags to '("+archive") makes the stock "a" key
>> in notmuch-emacs add the tag.
>
> That would be good. Add a patch for emacs to set that.

Posted as "[PATCH 0/2] Archive from notmuch-emacs with the archive
tag" [1]. Patch 1 sets notmuch-archive-tags to ("+archive" "-inbox"),
so "a" asks just archive to move the message and takes it out of the
inbox at once.

> Additionally, archived messages should have the inbox tag removed. So
> should replied, if that's not happening already.

Replied already loses inbox on trunk. mail-tag.sh gives a message
replied and removes inbox in the same rule. Sent mail never gets inbox.

Messages moved under archive/ lose inbox through "[PATCH v2 1/2]
notmuch: Tag messages under archive/ as archived" [2], which tags them
archived and removes inbox.

That left a gap between pressing "a" and running just archive. The
message is tagged archive but not yet moved, and mail-tag.sh put inbox
back on every notmuch new. Patch 2 of [1] closes it: mail-tag.sh now
drops inbox from anything tagged archive.

> inbox is mutually exclusive with sent, replied, archived.

With [1] and [2] applied, it is. Neither tag-derivation patch touches
replied or sent on an archived message, since your rule only
constrains inbox.

While checking this I found a gap in "[PATCH v2] mail: Add just
archive" [3]. v1 skipped drafts, but v2's search does not, so a draft
tagged archive would be moved out of drafts/. The fix is to add
"and not path:drafts/**" to the query. I'll fold it into v3 with the
flat-layout follow-up, unless you would rather fix it on apply.

